# SINGLE-TRACE EVALUATION MAPS, the trace (user 2026-11-06: "CAN YOU CREATE MAP
# FROM A SINGLE TRACE?" -> "I am talking about evaluations" -> "NO drive with new
# policy"): the evaluated policy's own deterministic explore trace, as the Gibson
# protocol's map comes from the agent's own exploration and maps_v30det came from
# v30's.
#
# il_trace_chw.env UNCHANGED -- c0's observation settings (MONO_CHW + SPEED_OBS),
# deterministic explore-mode driving, faults (crossing, off-road, collision) and
# the explore cap end a segment, and the next starts at the nearest drivable
# waypoint 3 m on from where the car stopped (the user's continuation rule), with
# run_trace's stuck and stall jumps -- with three changes:
#   TRACE_SPACING_M=0      EVERY env step is kept (0.1 s, ~0.4 m at c0's speed),
#                          not every 2 m, so the peer's 15 m MAD window holds ~37
#                          samples instead of ~7;
#   TRACE_COVERAGE=1.01    no early stop on coverage: the trace drives its whole
#                          distance budget (il_trace_step_<Town>.env), at least
#                          what v30det drove, and the coverage curve in index.json
#                          says whether it was still rising;
#   TRACE_MAX_STEPS        lifted so the distance budget is what ends it.
# NOT CHANGED, on purpose: TARGET_SPEED. The trace-speed rule (10 km/h,
# 2026-09-13) would change the speed feature c0 sees (SPEED_OBS); that is the
# user's decision, reported rather than applied.
. "$REPO/slurm/il_trace_chw.env"
export TRACE_SPACING_M=0 TRACE_COVERAGE=1.01 TRACE_MAX_STEPS=250000
